Subject: [PATCH] Fence terminal HDR10 analysis before starting the next source

A failure from the retiring source cannot become ready by polling it again.
Use the context's existing fenced stop/retry path without releasing a surface
still owned by the GPU or consuming the next source's prediction budget.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HDR10AISource.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HDR10AISource.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,10 @@
     const auto status = Collect();
     if (status != CB1_AI_READY)
     {
+      // Terminal work belongs to the retiring source. The context owner
+      // fences it before releasing its lease and starting the new source.
+      if (status != CB1_AI_PENDING)
+        return CB1_AI_INVALID;
       if (m_active && m_activation.Observe(status,Identity(binding),now) == Decision::Native)
       {
         m_fallback = true;
